[ZH] 也許其實會得到完全相反的觀察

99
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:59,300
[ZH] 就是也許其實第二個看似平靜的學生他才是目前有狀況的一位

100
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:02,300
[ZH] A regulated young person is fairly easy to spot.

101
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:09,200
[EN]  Breathing is steady, voices at normal pitch and pace, eye contact comes and goes naturally.

102
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:15,200
[EN]  They can follow a conversation, answer a question, and change their mind if you give them a good reason to.

103
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:22,200
[EN]  A rising state looks different, and it's often the state we miss because it doesn't look dramatic yet.

104
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:28,200
[EN]  Watch for faster, shallower breathing, a voice that gets louder, faster, or flatter,

105
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:31,740
[EN]  Fidgeting, pacing and sudden stillness

106
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:46,160
[ZH] 第一個如果是在一個很平衡調節的狀態下

